---
pre-compare: sort
---

// Synthetic PAN-OS records; every value is invented. The Traffic records follow
// the layout before PAN-OS 11.1, which ends with `offloaded` (115 columns): one
// connection that a policy dropped without a session, and one allowed UDP
// session that aged out. The System records follow the PAN-OS 11.1 System log
// fields. The firewall's clock is two hours ahead of UTC, which only the
// high-resolution timestamp states.
// https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/ngfw/administration/monitoring/use-syslog-for-monitoring/syslog-field-descriptions/traffic-log-fields
// https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/ngfw/administration/monitoring/use-syslog-for-monitoring/syslog-field-descriptions/system-log-fields
from_file env("TENZIR_INPUT") {
  read_lines
}
this = line.parse_syslog()
paloalto::ocsf::normalize
this = ocsf_cast(ocsf_derive(this))
select time, metadata.logged_time, class_name, activity_name, status, status_detail?, severity, count?, message?, connection_info?, unmapped
